{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-18T09:38:17.161Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"928e5cd9a3bda9591c204f9f","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-5kfzjh","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"workset:pm-5kfzjh+pm-gh1749","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-5kfzjh","claim:pm-gh1749","lineage:pm-5kfzjh","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.327","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-43p2c3"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GitHub managed-package update checks report git's command line and stderr as update_error instead of a stable code, and a timed-out ls-remote looks like any other failure"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found while fixing pm-5kfzjh. checkGithubUpdate in src/sdk/extension/update-check.ts reports error.message from runGitCommand as update_error, and the extension summary repeats it as update_check_reason. runGitCommand (src/sdk/extension/install-sources.ts) builds that message as \"Git command failed: git ls-remote <repository> <ref> <ref>^{}\" followed by git's stderr, or by execFile's own \"Command failed\" text. A GitHub update check therefore reports a multi-line string, not a stable code. Callers cannot branch on it, and it repeats git's stderr, which can name proxy hosts, credential helper prompts or local paths. A lookup killed by its budget is not told apart from a missing repository, the same gap pm-5kfzjh closed for npm. The npm path reports stable codes (npm_registry_lookup_failed, npm_registry_lookup_timed_out with update_check_timeout_ms). The GitHub path should do the same, with codes such as github_remote_lookup_failed and github_remote_lookup_timed_out, while keeping no_remote_reference_found and missing_installed_commit."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":3},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["diagnostics","extensions","github","stable-codes","update-check"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-18T09:38:17.161Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-18T09:38:17.161Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":60},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A failed GitHub update check reports a stable update_error code, never git's command line, repository URL or stderr; a git ls-remote lookup killed by its budget reports a distinct timed-out code and names the budget in update_check_timeout_ms, as the npm path does; unit tests cover the timeout, failure and success classifications; docs/PACKAGE_EVIDENCE.md lists the GitHub codes"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-ugqx"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A GitHub update check failure is a stable, private-data-free code that tells a timeout apart from an unavailable remote"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"update_error carries 'Git command failed: git ls-remote <repository> ...' plus git's stderr, and a timeout is indistinguishable from other failures"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"extensions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-5kfzjh","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-18T09:38:17.161Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"ddbfaea29f6c24f90071b458d13c175b22bea06c9404c21e1f5e4d25458fa46e","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d29215e7c8544ec96df1612a88f2fc1e444e48dacc35ffec36015e5b07e873f3"}
